{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation: phase 6, the continuation format and the row carrier\n     2\t\n     3\tStatus: **Companion design, phase 6 of `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`\n     4\t§10.** Written 2026-10-11 (Architect: claude-fable-5-1) from the frozen\n     5\tdesign as amended (`8f0b9e38`), the landed 4a evaluator\n     6\t(`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc`) and the 4b stage-1 evaluator\n     7\ton branch `srvm-phase4b` (read only), the merged phase-5 derivations\n     8\tdesign, the UCF document and its version-2 amendment, the row-carrier\n     9\tdraft (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`, body version 3, never landed),\n    10\tand the landed UCF code and harness (`src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc`,\n    11\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc`,\n    12\t`test/yin/vm/ucf/safepoint_harness_test.cljc`). The frozen document is\n    13\tnot changed by this one: §10 records findings with exact amendment text,\n    14\tfor the frozen design, for UCF, for the row-carrier draft and for\n    15\tcode-as-tuples. Subordinate to [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md),\n    16\tincluding its unitarity invariant, and to\n    17\t[`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`](./yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md)\n    18\t(\"the frozen design\"); format and rigor model:\n    19\t[`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.evaluator.md`](./yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.evaluator.md)\n    20\tand [`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md`](./yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md).\n    21\t\n    22\tEvery section marks its content **DECIDED** (an owner ruling, frozen\n    23\ttext, or code that exists) or **PROPOSED** (a design choice of this\n    24\tdocument, open to the reviewer). File references are to the worktree at\n    25\t`8f0b9e38`; line numbers are those of that commit; the 4b branch is\n    26\tcited as `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc`.\n    27\t\n    28\tContents: §0 rulings and the one-paragraph answer · §1 the canonical\n    29\tframe · §2 the row carrier: rows, window encoding, pending, captures,\n    30\tcontexts, census · §3 the frame validator · §4 layouts: how the stack\n    31\tand register kernels reconstruct canonical frames · §5 the safepoint\n    32\tharness · §6 code in the carrier: A and the tree association · §7\n    33\tlift and lower · §8 slices, gates and phase 7's entry conditions · §9\n    34\tverification honesty · §10 findings and amendments · §11 owner\n    35\tquestions · §12 portability.\n    36\t\n    37\t---\n    38\t\n    39\t## 0. Rulings and the one-paragraph answer\n    40\t\n    41\t### 0.1 Rulings that bind this design (DECIDED)\n    42\t\n    43\t1. **A is the only code identity**; new identities digest under Jing's\n    44\t   default (BLAKE3), never SHA-256 (`ucf/code-address` is\n    45\t   `jing/segment-key`, `ucf.cljc:247-251`).\n    46\t2. **No legacy**: one body version, no reader for older bodies, no\n    47\t   compat shim, no migration path; clean breaks.\n    48\t3. **Unitarity**: the AST is never lost and is always retrievable\n    49\t   wherever code is lowered; no design assumes a tree-less receiver; the\n    50\t   segment-to-tree association of the phase-5 design (§9.2 there:\n    51\t   `source-index`, `:yin.k/trees`) is a given.\n    52\t4. **The vector-to-datoms mapping is retired** (frozen §3.4 \"One vector\n    53\t   validator\"; code-as-tuples §7.2 superseded below); the carrier carries\n    54\t   positional tuples and rows, never datoms-from-vector.\n    55\t5. **dao.stream is the complexity boundary**: this design specifies no\n    56\t   transport mechanics; the carrier is data that crosses a stream.\n    57\t6. **One truth, many interpretations**: the register machine's\n    58\t   configuration `C = ⟨seg, pc, W⟩` with `E`, `K` is the canonical frame\n    59\t   shape; the stack and register kernels reconstruct it through their\n    60\t   layouts (frozen §4.3, §10 phase 6).\n    61\t7. **No file of phase 4b or phase 5 is touched**, so this phase runs\n    62\t   concurrently with them (§8.5 names the dependencies that remain).\n    63\t\n    64\t### 0.2 The answer\n    65\t\n    66\tA continuation is a value: one **canonical frame** of the register\n    67\tmachine, `act` or `tail`, with its saved window, its `K` of `:return`\n    68\tframes, its environment, its delivery record and its pending wait\n    69\t(frozen §2.4, §4.2), plus the task context it needs (store slice, module\n    70\tstores, parked table, cells, code by A, the tree association). Phase 6\n    71\tmakes that value exact and portable. **§1** restates the frame as the\n    72\t4b evaluator mints it. **§2** gives the row carrier: body version 3,\n    73\tMerkle content rows under Jing's default digest, one profile (the\n    74\tcanonical machine's contract `\"v4\"`), the window as a sorted keyed row\n    75\tin which a nil value is a present `[:lit nil]`, `:act`, `:tail`,\n    76\t`:window`, `:kframe`, `:reified` and `:parked-table` rows replacing the\n    77\tstale `:regs`/`:stack`/`:kframe`-with-stack-base rows, the pending rows\n    78\tunchanged in substance, the cell census unchanged. **§3** gives the\n    79\tframe validator as fourteen rules over the decoded canonical frame and\n    80\tthe carried code, independent of any engine: membership is recomputed\n    81\tfrom A (`saved(pc, rd)`), sites and destinations are checked against the\n    82\tinstruction at `pc−1`, return frames against the non-tail call they\n    83\tfollow. **§4** defines the two layouts: the register kernel's physical\n    84\tregister `locals + slot(v)` is read off the pair of images (A and R\n    85\tshare pcs), the stack kernel's operand stack within an activation is the\n    86\tsaved window in emission order, and both kernels' positional lexical\n    87\tframes become the named `E` through the owner chain of A. **§5** is the\n    88\tharness: every §4.1 row, both delivery modes, nested and reified\n    89\tcaptures, module contexts and every refusal, run on the\n    90\tsemantic-register kernel and, through their layouts, on the stack and\n    91\tregister kernels; the cross-engine law is that one program at one\n    92\tsafepoint yields **one canonical row set** on all three. **§6** fixes\n    93\twhat travels for code: canonical vectors keyed by A, the tree\n    94\tassociation, never a native image. **§8** cuts three slices and names\n    95\tphase 7's entry conditions.\n    96\t\n    97\t---\n    98\t\n    99\t## 1. The canonical frame\n   100\t\n   101\t### 1.1 Shapes, as the evaluator mints them\n   102\t\n   103\t**DECIDED** (frozen §2.4 \"Delivery\", §4.2; evaluator design §1.3-1.6;\n   104\t`srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:61-84` for `act-payload`,\n   105\t`tail-builders`; `:229-234` for the reified payload and the park). Two\n   106\tclosed state shapes and one closed delivery record:\n   107\t\n   108\t```clojure\n   109\tact  = {:segment seg :pc n :env E :window W :k K :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd r}}\n   110\ttail = {:segment seg :site n :k K :deliver {:deliver :return}}\n   111\tret  = {:type :return :segment seg :pc n :env E :window W :rd r}     ; one frame kind of K\n   112\t```\n   113\t\n   114\t- `:pc` of an `act` is the resume pc, already `pc+1` of the parking\n   115\t  instruction; `:site` of a `tail` is the tail call's own pc, provenance\n   116\t  only (evaluator §1.5).\n   117\t- `W` of an `act` is `saved(pc, rd) = W↾(L(pc) − {rd})`\n   118\t  (`analysis/saved`, `analysis.cljc:92-97`), built with `select-keys`,\n   119\t  so a nil-valued live register is a present key (frozen §4.2 \"dead\n   120\t  values never travel\"; evaluator §8 item 4).\n   121\t- `K` is a vector of `ret` frames, innermost last, or nil when empty\n   122\t  (`put-registers`, `semantic_register.cljc:47-52`); each frame's window\n   123\t  is `saved(frame.pc, frame.rd)` of its own body.\n   124\t- A **parked record** (`:park`, and FFI bookkeeping under a call id) is\n   125\t  an `act` payload plus `:type :parked-continuation :id` added by\n   126\t  `engine/park-continuation` (evaluator §1.6).\n   127\t- A **reified continuation** is `values/continuation owner (assoc act\n   128\t  :type :reified-continuation)` (`srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:229-232`).\n   129\t- The wait entry the engine holds is the `act` or `tail` payload plus\n   130\t  the engine's own fields (`:reason`, `:cursor-ref`, `:stream-id`,\n   131\t  `:datom`, `:call-id`, `:request-sent`, the link fields), which travel\n   132\t  as the **pending** (§2.4), never as frame slots.\n   133\t\n   134\t### 1.2 The UCF frame, keyed form\n   135\t\n   136\t**DECIDED** (frozen §4.2), restated with one naming decision (§10.1 F1):\n   137\t\n   138\t```clojure\n   139\t;; act state\n   140\t{:yin.k/state :act\n   141\t :yin.k/segment A  :yin.k/pc n\n   142\t :yin.k/env   {:yin.k/bindings {sym V …} :yin.k/store-of M?}\n   143\t :yin.k/window {r V …}                      ; exactly saved(pc, rd); sorted by r on the wire\n   144\t :yin.k/deliver {:yin.k/deliver :rd :yin.k/rd r}\n   145\t :yin.k/k [{:yin.k/frame-type :return :yin.k/segment A :yin.k/pc n\n   146\t            :yin.k/env E :yin.k/window {r V …} :yin.k/rd r} …]\n   147\t :yin.k/pending {…}}                        ; absent on a parked record and a reified value\n   148\t\n   149\t;; tail state\n   150\t{:yin.k/state :tail\n   151\t :yin.k/segment A  :yin.k/site n\n   152\t :yin.k/deliver {:yin.k/deliver :return}\n   153\t :yin.k/k [ … ]\n   154\t :yin.k/pending {…}}\n   155\t```\n   156\t\n   157\tThis keyed form is the **decoded canonical frame**: what the validator\n   158\tof §3 judges, what the layouts of §4 produce and consume, and what the\n   159\tharness compares across engines. The rows of §2 are its carrier and the\n   160\ttwo are in bijection (§2.6).\n   161\t\n   162\t---\n   163\t\n   164\t## 2. The row carrier\n   165\t\n   166\tThe row-carrier draft (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`) is adopted\n   167\t**except** where it describes the stack-shaped machine: its §2\n   168\t(positioning, four profiles), §5.2 (frame rows), §8 step 7 (frame\n   169\tchecks), the \"`v3` stamp does not move\" statements and §10.3-10.4\n   170\t(nested projection, contract stamp) are replaced here (§10.3 gives the\n   171\ttext). Its §3 (rows, id spaces, census), §4 (value union), §5.1 (value\n   172\trows), §5.3 (pending), §5.4 (task context), §5.5 (root), §6 (canonical\n   173\tcell numbering), §7 (equality) and §8 steps 1-6 and 8-12 stand, and are\n   174\trestated only where a slot changes.\n   175\t\n   176\t### 2.1 Positioning: body version 3, one profile\n   177\t\n   178\t**DECIDED** by ruling 2 (one version, no older bodies) and ruling 6\n   179\t(one canonical frame shape). The carrier is **body version 3**, the\n   180\tnumber the draft reserved and never landed; versions 0-2 are the old\n   181\thandoff's and are not read by the row reader (they leave with the\n   182\tstack-shaped machine at phase 8; until then they belong to\n   183\t`yin.vm.ucf.handoff`, untouched). The wire unit is the draft's:\n   184\t\n   185\t```clojure\n   186\t{:yin.k/handoff true  :yin.k/version 3  :yin.k/root T  :yin.k/rows [[id kind & slots] …]}\n   187\t```\n   188\t\n   189\t**PROPOSED.** The profile map a version-3 body carries is\n   190\t`{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}` and nothing else. There is\n   191\t**no `:yin.k/engine` key**: the frame is the canonical machine's and is\n   192\tengine-independent by ruling 6; the kernel that executes it is the\n   193\treceiving composition's choice (a semantic-register, stack or register\n   194\tkernel all lower the same rows through their layouts, §4). A body whose\n   195\tprofile map differs is `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`. The old four-profile\n   196\tregistry (`ucf/profiles`, `ucf.cljc:51-74`) describes version-2 bodies\n   197\tand is not consulted.\n   198\t\n   199\t### 2.2 Rows, ids, census\n   200\t\n   201\t**DECIDED** (draft §3, ruling 1). Every row is `[id kind & slots]`;\n   202\tcontent rows have `id = (jing/segment-key body)` under Jing's default\n   203\tdigest, the same call as `ucf/code-address`; identity rows are cells\n   204\t`:yin.k/c-<n>` numbered by the draft's §6 procedure; the root carries\n   205\tthe cell census `[X :cells C₁ B₁ …]`, `[Bᵢ :cell-body stream-cref position]`.\n   206\tContent rows reference children by id (crefs) in typed positions; a\n   207\t`[:row B]` position admits only its tabled kinds. One ordering rule:\n   208\t\"sorted\" is by the Jing canonical bytes of the key as spelled.\n   209\t\n   210\t### 2.3 The frame rows (replacing draft §5.2)\n   211\t\n   212\t**DECIDED** by frozen §4.2's last paragraph (\"`:regs` becomes\n   213\t`[segment-A pc env-cref window-cref k-cref deliver-D]` … a sibling\n   214\t`:tail-state [segment-A site k-cref deliver-D]` … `:window` is a keyed\n   215\trow `[r₁ V₁ r₂ V₂ …]` sorted by `r` … `:kframe` becomes\n   216\t`[segment-A pc env-cref window-cref rd]` … `:stack` and `stack-base`\n   217\tare removed\"). **PROPOSED** names `:act` and `:tail` for the two state\n   218\tkinds (§10.1 F1):\n   219\t\n   220\t| Kind | Slots | Notes |\n   221\t|---|---|---|\n   222\t| `:act` | `segment-A  pc-N  env-cref  window-cref  k-cref  rd-N` | an act state; the delivery record is `{:deliver :rd :rd rd-N}` by kind, so the kind is the discriminant and `rd` the one datum |\n   223\t| `:tail` | `segment-A  site-N  k-cref` | a tail state; delivery `{:deliver :return}` by kind; **no** env, window or pc slot (frozen §2.4 \"a `tail` state carries no window and no `E`\") |\n   224\t| `:window` | `r₁ V₁  r₂ V₂  …` sorted by `rᵢ` ascending, unique | the saved window; `rᵢ` is `N`; **a nil-valued register is present as `rᵢ [:lit nil]`**; the empty window is `[:window]` |\n   225\t| `:k` | `kframe-cref …` outermost first (bottom to top) | `K`; `[:k]` is the empty continuation |\n   226\t| `:kframe` | `segment-A  pc-N  env-cref  window-cref  rd-N` | one `:return` frame; `pc` is the resume pc after a non-tail call |\n   227\t| `:wait` | `state-cref  pending-cref` | a blocked wait: `state-cref` is an `:act` or a `:tail` row |\n   228\t| `:reified` | `act-cref` | a captured continuation value (replaces the draft's `[:reified regs-cref]`); its act's `pc−1` is a `:current-continuation` |\n   229\t| `:parked-ref` | `parked-id-P` | unchanged: resolves in the parked table |\n   230\t| `:env` | `bindings-cref  store-of` | unchanged (draft §5.1): `store-of` is `M` or nil |\n   231\t| `:bindings` | `S₁ V₁  S₂ V₂ …` sorted by symbol | unchanged |\n   232\t\n   233\tThe window row is structural, never a `V`: it is always a row even when\n   234\tit reaches no reference (the draft's \"a reference-free collection must be\n   235\t`[:lit d]`\" rule is about guest collections, §4 of the draft, and does\n   236\tnot apply to `:window`, `:bindings`, `:store` or any other tabled keyed\n   237\trow). `rd` is carried on `:act` so that the frozen §4.2 \"destination\n   238\tequality\" rule (§3 rule 6) has something to compare: it must equal the\n   239\tdestination of the instruction at `pc−1` and is therefore redundant data\n   240\tthat the validator checks, exactly as `pc` is redundant with the pending\n   241\tand checked.\n   242\t\n   243\t### 2.4 Pending rows\n   244\t\n   245\t**DECIDED** (draft §5.3, UCF §7.4.3, v2 amendment §2): one kind\n   246\t`:pending`, first slot the reason, remaining slots fixed per reason;\n   247\treasons `:next :put :ffi :ffi-request :link-request :link-response\n   248\t:install`; `:park` and `:call-effect` are not reasons (ucf-revisions §8).\n   249\tUnchanged from the draft:\n   250\t\n   251\t| reason | slots after the reason |\n   252\t|---|---|\n   253\t| `:next` | `cell-C` |\n   254\t| `:put` | `stream-cref  value-V  op-id-D` |\n   255\t| `:ffi` | `cell-C  call-id-D  op` |\n   256\t| `:ffi-request` | `call-id-D  envelope-V  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  response-cell-C  op-id-D` |\n   257\t| `:link-request` | `link-id-D  name-S  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  cell-C  envelope-D  op-id-D` |\n   258\t| `:link-response` | `link-id-D  name-S  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  cell-C` |\n   259\t| `:install` | `name-S` (never sufficient alone: the root's installs slot holds the entry) |\n   260\t\n   261\tWhat changes is only **which state a pending rides on**: a `:wait` row\n   262\tpairs a pending with an `:act` (write-result delivery) **or a `:tail`**\n   263\t(through-return delivery), the frozen §4.1 table's two state columns.\n   264\tThe retained FFI request keeps the 4b evaluator's in-VM markers out of\n   265\tthe frame: `:request-sent`, `:call-id`, `:op`, `:datom`, `:response-cursor`\n   266\tand `:response-stream` are the pending's, as today\n   267\t(`handoff.cljc:702-724`, `:3219-3229`).\n   268\t\n   269\t### 2.5 Captures, parked records, module contexts\n   270\t\n   271\t**DECIDED** (frozen §2.4 \"current-continuation\", \"park\"; evaluator §1.6;\n   272\tdraft §5.1, §5.4).\n   273\t\n   274\t- A **reified continuation** value is `[:row B]` where `B` is a\n   275\t  `:reified [act-cref]` row; the act has no pending, its `pc−1` is a\n   276\t  `:current-continuation`, its `rd` is that instruction's destination,\n   277\t  and its window is `saved(pc, rd)` (so it is never captured inside its\n   278\t  own destination, frozen §2.4).\n   279\t- The **parked table** is `[:parked-table P₁ state-cref₁ P₂ state-cref₂ …]`\n   280\t  sorted by `P`, each state an `:act` (an explicit park: `pc−1` is\n   281\t  `:park`) **or**, for FFI bookkeeping under a live `:ffi`/`:ffi-request`\n   282\t  pending whose call id is `P`, an `:act` whose `pc−1` is the `:ffi-call`,\n   283\t  or a `:tail` whose site is the effectful tail `:call` (evaluator §1.6:\n   284\t  \"the `tail`-shaped FFI parked record is specified for closure of the\n   285\t  shape set\"). A root of kind `:parked` names its active record by\n   286\t  `parked-id`; an active parked id may never select a bookkeeping record\n   287\t  (v2 amendment §7.3, kept).\n   288\t- A **module context** is `E`'s `store-of`: an `:env` row whose second\n   289\t  slot is `M`; the module store travels once as `[:module-store M store-cref]`\n   290\t  (draft §5.4), and every `store-of` must resolve to a carried module\n   291\t  store (draft §8 step 3). Closures carry `store-of` in their `:closure`\n   292\t  row as today.\n   293\t- **Install children** are whole `:task` rows in the child role (draft\n   294\t  §5.4, §5.5), unchanged; a child's frames are `:wait` rows of the same\n   295\t  grammar.\n   296\t\n   297\t### 2.6 The bijection with the keyed frame\n   298\t\n   299\t**PROPOSED.** `rows->frame` and `frame->rows` are two pure functions\n   300\t(`yin.vm.ucf.rows`, §8.1) and `frame->rows ∘ rows->frame = id` on valid\n   301\trow sets, `rows->frame ∘ frame->rows = id` on canonical keyed frames:\n   302\t`:act` ↔ `{:yin.k/state :act …}` with `:yin.k/deliver {:yin.k/deliver :rd\n   303\t:yin.k/rd rd}` synthesised from the kind and the `rd` slot; `:tail` ↔\n   304\t`{:yin.k/state :tail …}` with `{:yin.k/deliver :return}`; `:window` ↔\n   305\t`:yin.k/window` as a map (`[:lit nil]` ↔ a nil-valued key); `:k` ↔\n   306\t`:yin.k/k` in order. The validator (§3) runs on the keyed form after\n   307\t`rows->frame`, which only reshapes and never decides anything the\n   308\tvalidator decides.\n   309\t\n   310\t---\n   311\t\n   312\t## 3. The frame validator\n   313\t\n   314\t### 3.1 Inputs and independence\n   315\t\n   316\t**DECIDED** (frozen §4.2: \"The window's membership is validated, not\n   317\ttrusted: the receiver recomputes `saved(pc, rd)` from A … the full frame\n   318\tvalidator also checks representation, body scope, site/pc pairing,\n   319\tdestination equality, delivery mode, return-frame sites, `K` structure,\n   320\tand pending compatibility with `reason`\"). The validator is a pure\n   321\tfunction\n   322\t\n   323\t```clojure\n   324\t(frame/defect frame code)   ; frame: a decoded canonical frame (§1.2)\n   325\t                            ; code:  {A vector}, every vector code/well-formed?\n   326\t;; => nil, or {:yin.k/kind k :yin.k/path p …}\n   327\t```\n   328\t\n   329\tin **PROPOSED** namespace `yin.vm.semantic-register.frame`, file\n   330\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc`, requiring only\n   331\t`yin.vm.semantic-register.code` (`body-ranges`, `body-index`, `rd`,\n   332\t`tail-call?`, `registers`-per-body via `parse`),\n   333\t`yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis` (`analyze`, `saved`) and `yin.vm`\n   334\t(`reserved-name?`). It knows no kernel, no engine, no stream: a frame a\n   335\tstack kernel lifted and a frame the register evaluator lifted are judged\n   336\tby the same function on the same inputs.\n   337\t\n   338\t### 3.2 The rules\n   339\t\n   340\tRules run in order; the first defect wins; every defect carries\n   341\t`:yin.k/kind` and `:yin.k/path` (the frame key path, `[:yin.k/k i …]` for\n   342\ta return frame). `a = (analysis/analyze v)` is computed once per segment.\n   343\t\"The instruction at `pc−1`\" is `(nth v (dec pc))`; `body(p)` is\n   344\t`(code/body-index (code/body-ranges v) p)`; `k(body)` is the body's\n   345\tregister count (`code/parse`'s `:registers`).\n   346\t\n   347\t| # | Rule | Refusal kind |\n   348\t|---|---|---|\n   349\t| 1 | **Shape.** An `act` has exactly `:yin.k/state :yin.k/segment :yin.k/pc :yin.k/env :yin.k/window :yin.k/deliver :yin.k/k` and optionally `:yin.k/pending`; a `tail` exactly `:yin.k/state :yin.k/segment :yin.k/site :yin.k/deliver :yin.k/k` and optionally `:yin.k/pending`; no other key; `:yin.k/state` is `:act` or `:tail` | `:frame-shape` |\n   350\t| 2 | **Segment.** `:yin.k/segment` names a key of `code`; the same for every return frame's segment | `:segment` |\n   351\t| 3 | **Bounds.** `pc` is an exact integer with `0 < pc < (count v)`; a return frame's `pc` likewise; a `tail`'s `site` with `0 ≤ site < (count v)` | `:pc-bounds` |\n   352\t| 4 | **Window representation.** `:yin.k/window` is a map whose keys are exact non-negative integers (on the wire: sorted ascending, unique); values are `V`; a nil value is a present key | `:window-representation` |\n   353\t| 5 | **Body scope.** every window key is `< k(body(pc))` and `body(pc)` is the body of `pc−1` (a resume pc never crosses a body boundary: `pc−1` and `pc` are in one body, which holds because no body ends in a parking instruction, frozen §3.4 rule 6) | `:window-scope` |\n   354\t| 6 | **Site.** the instruction at `pc−1` of an `act` is one of `:stream-next :stream-put :ffi-call :call :park :current-continuation`, and for a `:call` it is **not** a tail call (`code/tail-call?` false); a `tail`'s `site` instruction is a `:call` with `tail?` true | `:site` |\n   355\t| 7 | **Destination.** `(:yin.k/rd (:yin.k/deliver act))` equals `(code/rd (nth v (dec pc)))` | `:destination` |\n   356\t| 8 | **Membership.** `(set (keys window)) = (analysis/saved a pc rd)`: a key outside the set is `:window-extra`, a member missing is `:window-missing`, `rd` present is `:window-self` (checked before the set comparison so it is named separately) | `:window-extra` / `:window-missing` / `:window-self` |\n   357\t| 9 | **Delivery mode.** an `act`'s deliver is exactly `{:yin.k/deliver :rd :yin.k/rd r}` with `r` an exact integer; a `tail`'s exactly `{:yin.k/deliver :return}`; a `tail` has no `:yin.k/window`, `:yin.k/env` or `:yin.k/pc` (rule 1 already) | `:deliver` |\n   358\t| 10 | **Return frames.** `:yin.k/k` is a vector; each frame has exactly `:yin.k/frame-type :return :yin.k/segment :yin.k/pc :yin.k/env :yin.k/window :yin.k/rd`; the instruction at `frame.pc−1` in `frame.segment` is a `:call` with `tail?` false; `frame.rd` equals that call's `rd`; `(set (keys frame.window)) = (analysis/saved aₛ frame.pc frame.rd)` in that segment's analysis, with the three membership kinds as rule 8; window keys `< k(body(frame.pc))` | `:return-site` / `:return-destination` / `:return-window-*` |\n   359\t| 11 | **Environment.** `:yin.k/env` (of an `act` and of every return frame) is `{:yin.k/bindings {S V …}}` optionally with `:yin.k/store-of M`; every binding key is a symbol and none is `yin/def` (Rule R; `vm/reserved-name?`) | `:env` / `:reserved-name` |\n   360\t| 12 | **Reason compatibility.** when `:yin.k/pending` is present, its reason is admitted by the instruction at `pc−1` (`act`) or `site` (`tail`): `:stream-next` → `:next`; `:stream-put` → `:put`; `:ffi-call` → `:ffi` or `:ffi-request`; `:call` → `:next :put :ffi :ffi-request :link-request :link-response :install`; `:park` and `:current-continuation` admit **no** pending (frozen §4.1; `wire-of-kind`, `handoff.cljc:491-504`; ucf-revisions §8: the static kind gates, the observed reason decides) | `:reason-mismatch` |\n   361\t| 13 | **Captured context.** when the frame is judged as a reified value (`context :captured`): it is an `act`, has no pending, and `pc−1` is `:current-continuation` | `:captured-site` |\n   362\t| 14 | **Parked context.** when judged as a parked-table entry (`context :parked`): an `act` whose `pc−1` is `:park` and no pending; or, when the table key is the call id of a live `:ffi`/`:ffi-request` pending of the same task, an `act` whose `pc−1` is `:ffi-call` or a `tail` whose site's call is the parking call (bookkeeping) | `:parked-site` |\n   363\t\n   364\tThe validator takes a `context` argument, one of `:wait`, `:captured`,\n   365\t`:parked`, selecting rules 12-14. Rule 8 is the frozen §4.2 membership\n   366\tcheck; rules 5, 10 and 12 are its \"body scope\", \"return-frame sites\" and\n   367\t\"pending compatibility\"; rules 6-7 its \"site/pc pairing\" and\n   368\t\"destination equality\"; rule 9 \"delivery mode\". Nothing here reads\n   369\t`:yin.k/live`, a stack depth or a stack base: those were the stack\n   370\tmachine's (v2 amendment §5.1-5.3) and have no counterpart.\n   371\t\n   372\t### 3.3 Where the validator runs\n   373\t\n   374\t**DECIDED** (draft §8 step 7, replaced; §10.3). On lower, after the\n   375\tgate, structure, graph and hash steps (draft §8 steps 1-4) and before\n   376\tcanonical numbering, **every** `:act`, `:tail`, `:kframe`, `:reified`\n   377\tand parked-table state is decoded to its keyed frame and judged by\n   378\t`frame/defect` with its context; a defect is `:yin.k/undecodable` with\n   379\tthe rule's kind and the row path. On lift, the same function runs over\n   380\tevery frame the lift assembled before any row is emitted (a frame the\n   381\tevaluator itself minted that fails is `:yin.k/non-portable` kind\n   382\t`:inconsistent-state`, the existing kind). The harness (§5) also runs it\n   383\tover every frame a layout reconstructs.\n   384\t\n   385\t---\n   386\t\n   387\t## 4. Layouts: reconstructing the canonical frame\n   388\t\n   389\t### 4.1 What a layout is\n   390\t\n   391\t**DECIDED** (frozen §4.3; UCF §7.4.2). A foreign engine keeps a static\n   392\tsafepoint map per segment and engine with `:yin.safepoint/segment A`,\n   393\t`:yin.safepoint/pc`, `:yin.safepoint/engine`, the per-pc `def`, `use`,\n   394\t`L(pc)` derived from A (`analysis/analyze`), `lexically-required`, and\n   395\t`:yin.safepoint/layout`, \"a map from physical location to virtual\n   396\tregister\". Its obligation: from its physical state at a safepoint,\n   397\tproduce the canonical frame (`A`, resume `pc`, every register in\n   398\t`saved(pc, rd)`, `E`, `K` with each frame's window and `rd`, the delivery\n   399\trecord, the pending, the store context) for an `act`; `A`, `site`, `K`,\n   400\tdelivery, pending for a `tail`; and `lift(lower(frame)) = frame` on\n   401\tadmitted canonical frames.\n   402\t\n   403\tTwo kernels are intended to reconstruct canonical frames in phase 6:\n   404\tthe de Bruijn register kernel over `R(A)` and the de Bruijn stack kernel\n   405\tover `H(A)`, both images being pure functions of A (phase 5). The AST\n   406\twalker is **not** (frozen §10 phase 6 names the three kernels; the\n   407\twalker has no pc and is the oracle of the evaluator, not a frame\n   408\treconstructor).\n   409\t\n   410\t**PROPOSED** namespace `yin.vm.semantic-register.layout`, file\n   411\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc`, requiring\n   412\t`yin.vm.semantic-register.code`, `.analysis`, `.derive` (phase 5:\n   413\t`register-image`, `stack-image`, `resolve`), `yin.vm.debruijn`\n   414\t(`resolve-name`), `yin.vm.engine` (`bind-params`), and the two kernels'\n   415\tpublic state accessors. Four public functions:\n   416\t`register-layout`, `stack-layout` (static, per segment),\n   417\t`lift-frame` and `lower-frame` (per kernel, dispatching on the kernel's\n   418\t`link-format`).\n   419\t\n   420\t### 4.2 The register kernel's layout\n   421\t\n   422\t**DECIDED** by the phase-5 design §2.4 (\"Layout is A's: bodies and pcs\n   423\tare identical to the vector's\") and §2.3 (`R(v) = locals + slot(v)`).\n   424\t\n   425\t*Static half.* For a segment `A` with register image `R =\n   426\t(:image (derive/register-image v))`, the layout is read off the **pair**\n   427\t`(v, R)` pc by pc, without any access to the allocator's internals: for\n   428\tevery pc `p`, the tuple `v[p]` names virtual registers in its `rd`,\n   429\t`:reg` and `:regs` slots (`code/rd`, `code/uses`) and `R[p]` names the\n   430\tcorresponding physical registers in the same slots (same mnemonic, same\n   431\toperand positions, one `live` operand appended on boundary opcodes). So\n   432\t\n   433\t```\n   434\tphys(body, v) = the physical register paired with virtual v at any pc of body\n   435\t```\n   436\t\n   437\tis a total function on the virtual registers a body names (every minted\n   438\tid with a syntactic definition appears as some instruction's `rd`; a\n   439\tdefinition-less id appears as a layout-syntax operand and pairs with the\n   440\tstructural slot). The layout publishes, per body, `virt→phys` and its\n   441\tinverse `phys→virt` on the image of `virt→phys`; a physical slot with\n   442\ttwo virtual preimages at one pc is impossible (one tuple, one slot), and\n   443\ttwo virtuals sharing a slot is the allocator's reuse across disjoint\n   444\tintervals, so `phys→virt` is **per pc**: `phys→virt(p, s) = the v with\n   445\tphys(v) = s and p ∈ [start(v), end(v)]`, computed from `analysis/live`\n   446\twithout any interval machinery as \"the `v ∈ L(p) ∪ def(p−1)` with\n   447\t`phys(v) = s`\"; uniqueness at each `p` is a property the harness\n   448\tchecks (§5.6 item 3), never assumed.\n   449\t\n   450\t*Dynamic half, lift.* The register kernel's wait entry at a boundary\n   451\t(`yin.vm.debruijn.register`'s payload: `:image`, `:site-pc`, `:pc`,\n   452\t`:frames`, `:regs [[s V] …]`, `:live [s …]`, `:continuation [{:site-pc\n   453\t:return-pc :frames :regs :live :dest} …]`, `:dest`, `:resume-mode`,\n   454\t`:store-of`; v2 amendment §5.3, `handoff.cljc:945-980`) reconstructs:\n   455\t\n   456\t- `A` = the image's A (the kernel's `:image` identity is R under the old\n   457\t  contract; after phase 5 the kernel's code space is keyed by A with R as\n   458\t  checksum, phase-5 §7.6; the layout maps the image row to its A).\n   459\t- `pc` = the payload's `pc` **relative to the image** (the kernel\n   460\t  concatenates images with offsets; `absolute-pc`/`image-row`,\n   461\t  `debruijn/register.cljc:326-337`); R's pcs are A's, so the relative pc\n   462\t  is the canonical pc.\n   463\t- `rd` = `(code/rd v[pc−1])`; `:resume-mode :write-result` ↔ `act`,\n   464\t  `:return-result` (a tail `:call`, `dest nil`) ↔ `tail`.\n   465\t- `W` = `{phys→virt(pc, s) ↦ V : [s V] ∈ regs}`. The kernel's `live`\n   466\t  operand is the physical image of `L(pc) − {rd}` by phase-5 §2.5, so the\n   467\t  key set equals `saved(pc, rd)`; the validator's rule 8 checks it.\n   468\t- `E` = §4.4 from `frames` and the owner chain at `pc`.\n   469\t- `K` = each continuation frame `{site-pc return-pc regs dest frames}` ↦\n   470\t  `{:return A pc=return-pc rd=dest window=(regs through phys→virt at\n   471\t  return-pc) env=(frames through §4.4 at return-pc)}`.\n   472\t- pending: the engine fields, exactly as today's lift maps them\n   473\t  (`lift-pending!`, `handoff.cljc:674-749`).\n   474\t\n   475\t*Dynamic half, lower.* The inverse: `regs = [[phys(v) V] …]` for `v` in\n   476\tthe window, sorted by physical index; `live` = the sorted physical keys\n   477\t(the kernel's validator then recomputes `body-liveness` and must agree,\n   478\t`live-exact-rule`); `frames` from `E` by §4.4; `dest = phys(rd)`;\n   479\t`resume-mode` by state kind; continuation frames likewise; `:image` the\n   480\trow of `A`; `:site-pc = pc−1`.\n   481\t\n   482\t### 4.3 The stack kernel's layout\n   483\t\n   484\t**DECIDED** by the phase-5 design §3.2 (the stack emitter's walk) and\n   485\tthe frozen §8.3 remark about pushes; **PROPOSED** as a layout.\n   486\t\n   487\t*Static half.* `H = (:image (derive/stack-image v))`. Two tables per\n   488\tsegment:\n   489\t\n   490\t1. **pc correspondence.** The stack emitter visits parse nodes in the\n   491\t   same order as `project` (children, then the parent; bodies FIFO) and\n   492\t   emits one instruction per A instruction **plus** a `:push` after each\n   493\t   child of a call, `:stream-put` target or `:ffi-call` operand. So the\n   494\t   sequence of H instructions **with every `:push` removed** is in\n   495\t   one-to-one order correspondence with A's instructions: the k-th\n   496\t   non-push H instruction corresponds to A's pc `k`. `h->a` and `a->h`\n   497\t   are the two directions of that zip. The harness checks the mnemonic\n   498\t   families agree at every k (§5.6 item 4); the design does not rely on\n   499\t   the claim without the check.\n   500\t2. **operand-stack layout.** For an A pc `p` that is a parking\n   501\t   instruction, `stack-layout(p)` is the vector of virtual registers\n   502\t   whose values the activation's operand stack holds, bottom to top,\n   503\t   when control is at `a->h(p)`: walking the parse tree from the body's\n   504\t   root to the node at `p`, for each ancestor `n` and the child `c` on\n   505\t   the path, the pushed-and-unconsumed children of `n` before `c` are:\n   506\t   for a `:call`, the operator and the operands before `c`; for a\n   507\t   `:stream-put`, the target when `c` is the value; for an `:ffi-call`,\n   508\t   the operands before `c`; for `:if`, `:define`, `:stream-cursor`,\n   509\t   `:stream-next`, `:stream-close`, `:resume`, none (their child is\n   510\t   consumed directly). The vector lists those children's `rd`s in that\n   511\t   order.\n   512\t\n   513\t   **Property checked, not assumed** (§5.6 item 5): `(set\n   514\t   (stack-layout p)) = (analysis/saved a (inc p) (code/rd v[p]))`. The\n   515\t   argument: the registers live after a parking instruction are exactly\n   516\t   the already-evaluated siblings that an enclosing expression will\n   517\t   still read, which are exactly what has been pushed and not yet\n   518\t   consumed; the two worked cases are `(f (g x) y)` at the inner call\n   519\t   (stack `[f]`, `saved(4, 2) = {1}`, `analysis_test.cljc:131-139`) and\n   520\t   `(f (if c (g) 2) y)` at `(g)` (stack `[f]`; `saved = {1}` since the\n   521\t   `if`'s `rd` is the call's own `rd`).\n   522\t\n   523\t*Dynamic half, lift.* The stack kernel's wait entry (`:image`, `:pc`,\n   524\t`:frames`, `:stack`, `:continuation [{:return-pc :frames :stack-base\n   525\t:store-of} …]`, `:store-of`; v2 amendment §5.2, `handoff.cljc:897-924`)\n   526\treconstructs: `A` the image's; canonical `pc = h->a(pc_H − 1) + 1`; `rd\n   527\t= (code/rd v[pc−1])`; `W` = zip of `stack-layout(pc−1)` with the\n   528\tactivation's operand-stack slice (from the innermost frame's\n   529\t`stack-base` to the top), key `rdᵢ` ↦ value; `E` by §4.4; `K` = each\n   530\tcontinuation frame ↦ `{:return A pc=h->a(return-pc_H − 1)+1 rd=(code/rd\n   531\tv[pc−1]) window=(zip of stack-layout at that call with the slice\n   532\t[stack-base_i, stack-base_{i+1}) of the operand stack) env=§4.4}`; state\n   533\tkind: `act` unless the parking H instruction is a `:call` with `tail?`\n   534\ttrue, then `tail` with `site = h->a(pc_H − 1)`. A `tail` state has no\n   535\toperand slice of its own: the tail call popped its operands and no value\n   536\tof the current body is read again (frozen §2.4), so the stack kernel's\n   537\tstack at a tail-call park is exactly the enclosing frames' slices.\n   538\t\n   539\t*Dynamic half, lower.* Operand stack = concatenation over `K` outermost\n   540\tfirst of each frame's window laid out by `stack-layout` at its call,\n   541\tthen the current activation's window laid out at `pc−1`; `stack-base`s\n   542\tare the running lengths; `pc_H = a->h(pc−1) + 1`; `frames` by §4.4.\n   543\t\n   544\t### 4.4 Positional lexical frames and the named environment\n   545\t\n   546\t**DECIDED** by frozen §2.1 (\"Parameters live in E, not in registers …\n   547\tleaves the de Bruijn register image free to map parameters to its own\n   548\t`L` bank\") and §2.4 (`E_c[ps ↦ a]` by `bind-params`); phase-5 §1.2 (the\n   549\towner chain). Both de Bruijn kernels hold the lexical environment as\n   550\tpositional frames `F = [[V …] …]` outermost first, one per enclosing\n   551\tclosure activation, plus a task-wide free environment (v2 amendment §2).\n   552\tThe canonical `E` at a pc of body `b` is\n   553\t\n   554\t```\n   555\tE = (merge free-env\n   556\t           (bind-params params(owner-chain[0]) F[0])      ; outermost closure first\n   557\t           …\n   558\t           (bind-params params(owner-chain[last]) F[last]))  ; the current body's own\n   559\t     ∪ {engine/store-of-key M}  when the activation's closure carries store-of M\n   560\t```\n   561\t\n   562\twhere `params(c)` is the `:closure` tuple's parameter vector in A\n   563\t(`(nth v c 2)`) for each closure pc on the owner chain of `b`, outermost\n   564\tfirst (phase-5 §1.2's `chain` reversed), and `bind-params` is the\n   565\tengine's (`engine/bind-params`: rightmost duplicate wins, nil-fill,\n   566\textra arguments dropped). This reproduces exactly the `E` the register\n   567\tevaluator builds on closure entry (`semantic_register.cljc:141-143`:\n   568\t`(merge (:env c) (bind-params (:params c) args))`), because `(:env c)`\n   569\tis the creating activation's `E`, which is itself free-env merged with\n   570\tthe outer chain's bindings. The inverse (`E` → `F`) reads `F[i] =\n   571\t(mapv #(get E %) params(chain[i]))`, which loses nothing the kernel\n   572\tneeds: a parameter shadowed by an inner frame is still read from its own\n   573\tframe by depth, and the de Bruijn kernels never read a name.\n   574\t\n   575\t**Checked, not assumed** (§5.6 item 6): the harness compares the `E` a\n   576\tlayout reconstructs with the `E` the register evaluator holds at the\n   577\tsame safepoint of the same program, for every corpus program, including\n   578\t`:duplicate-param` (`(fn [x x] x)`) and `:nested-closure`.\n   579\t\n   580\t*Closure values.* A de Bruijn closure value (positional marker: segment,\n   581\timage-relative entry, arity, frames `F`, store-of) reconstructs to the\n   582\tcanonical closure (`{:type :closure :params :entry :segment :env}`,\n   583\tevaluator §1.8): `params` from A's `:closure` tuple at the entry's owner\n   584\tpc, `env` by the rule above over the closure's captured `F`, `entry` the\n   585\tbody pc (A's pc). The inverse is `module/lift-closure`'s positional\n   586\tmarker with `F` read back from `env` by the chain. The harness item 7\n   587\tchecks both directions on the `\"closure value\"` and `\"higher order\"` B0\n   588\trows.\n   589\t\n   590\t### 4.5 What a layout never does\n   591\t\n   592\t**DECIDED.** A layout reads a kernel's state and A; it never runs code,\n   593\tnever consults the receiver's store or free-env to fill a binding\n   594\t(`E`'s free-env part is the **task's own** carried free environment,\n   595\t`:free-env` of the body when the source was a de Bruijn kernel, the\n   596\t`:env` the semantic-register task started with otherwise; §6.3), never\n   597\treads a native image's hash as an identity (A is the key; H and R are\n   598\tchecksums), and never invents a safepoint: a kernel pc that is not a\n   599\tcanonical safepoint successor is `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` (UCF §7.4.2).\n   600\t\n   601\t---\n   602\t\n   603\t## 5. The safepoint harness\n   604\t\n   605\t### 5.1 What it proves\n   606\t\n   607\t**DECIDED** (frozen §10 phase 6 gate; UCF §7.11 \"Safepoint conformance\n   608\tharness\"; §7.11.1 \"Safepoint reconstruction\"). For every row of the\n   609\tfrozen §4.1 table, both delivery modes, nested and reified captures,\n   610\tmodule contexts and every refusal: lift at the safepoint, lower into a\n   611\tfresh machine, continue, and the result and effect trace equal the\n   612\tuninterrupted reference run; `lift(lower(frame)) = frame`; the frame's\n   613\treason is the observed wait's. **For every engine intended to\n   614\treconstruct canonical frames**: the semantic-register kernel, the stack\n   615\tkernel through §4.3, the register kernel through §4.2.\n   616\t\n   617\t### 5.2 Rows\n   618\t\n   619\tEach row is a program shape, a way to park it, and a way to satisfy its\n   620\twait, built as `safepoint_harness_test.cljc` builds its rows today\n   621\t(`:117-304`) over the register-shaped evaluator and the two de Bruijn\n   622\tkernels fed `derive/stack-image` and `derive/register-image` of\n   623\t`project`'s vector. The corpus wraps each parking expression in four\n   624\tsegments as today (`:92-106`: bare, as an operand, three activations\n   625\tdeep, inside a closure with a captured environment), so every row is\n   626\texercised with an empty `K`, a non-empty `K`, and a non-trivial `E`.\n   627\t\n   628\t| Row | Parking instruction | State | Delivery | Pending | Template today |\n   629\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   630\t| blocked read | `:stream-next` | act | rd | `:next` | `read-row` (`:117-133`) |\n   631\t| blocked write | `:stream-put` | act | rd | `:put` with the retained value | `write-row` (`:136-153`) |\n   632\t| FFI sent | `:ffi-call` → ok | act | rd | `:ffi` with the kept response cell | `sent-ffi-row` (`:168-183`) |\n   633\t| FFI retained | `:ffi-call` → full | act | rd | `:ffi-request` with the envelope and both routes | `retained-ffi-row` (`:186-206`) |\n   634\t| effectful call, non-tail, stream | `:call` of `stream/next!` | act | rd | `:next` | `stream-call-row false` (`:251-270`) |\n   635\t| **effectful call, tail, stream** | tail `:call` of `stream/next!` | **tail** | **return** | `:next` | `stream-call-row true` |\n   636\t| link request / response, non-tail | `:call` of `require` | act | rd | `:link-request` then `:link-response` | `require-row false` (`:220-244`) at both phases |\n   637\t| **link, tail** | tail `:call` of `require` | **tail** | **return** | `:link-request`, `:link-response` | `require-row true` |\n   638\t| install, non-tail and tail | `:call` of `require` while the child runs | act / tail | rd / return | `:install` + the root's install entry with the child task | new: park the child (its body reads a stream) so the install is live at export (`parked-installer`, `v2_support.cljc:453`) |\n   639\t| explicit park | `:park` | parked record (act) | rd | none; root kind `:parked` | `park-row` (`:273-283`) |\n   640\t| reified capture | `:current-continuation` then a park | a `:reified` value in `W` or `E`; `pc−1` is the capture site | rd | the enclosing park's | new: `(let [k (current-continuation)] (f k (stream-next c)))`, so the capture is live in the window of the blocked read; also the capture **invoked after lower** |\n   641\t| nested capture | a reified value whose own window holds a reified value | | | | new |\n   642\t| module context | a closure defined in a linked module parks inside its body | act with `store-of` in `E` | rd | `:next` | `parked-module-store-cursors` (`lift_support.cljc:310`) |\n   643\t| halt | `:halt` / `:return` with empty `K` | result | | | `halt-row` (`:286-290`) |\n   644\t| **tail-effect halt** | a deferred tail completion whose `K` is empty halts on delivery | tail | return | `:next` | new: `((fn [c] (stream/next! c)) cursor)` in tail position at the root; the lowered task halts with the delivered value and an env free of `store-of` (evaluator §2.2 F2) |\n   645\t\n   646\tRefusal rows: `:yin.k/not-quiescent` (a woken reader in the ready queue,\n   647\t`a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent`, `:591-603`);\n   648\t`:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` (a layout asked to lift a kernel at a pc whose\n   649\t`pc−1` is not a parking instruction: constructed by stepping the register\n   650\tkernel one instruction past a `:const` and asking `lift-frame`);\n   651\t`:yin.k/non-portable :reason-mismatch` (the D4 `:observe` hold,\n   652\t`a-held-immediate-refuses-export`, `:675-692`); and the **frame\n   653\tvalidator's own** refusals on tampered rows: a window with an extra key\n   654\t(`:window-extra`), a missing live key (`:window-missing`), the\n   655\tdestination present (`:window-self`), a wrong `rd` (`:destination`), a\n   656\treturn frame after a tail call (`:return-site`), a reason the site does\n   657\tnot admit (`:reason-mismatch`), a `:tail` row carrying a window\n   658\t(`:frame-shape`), a nil-valued key dropped from a window\n   659\t(`:window-missing`, the portability canary), a reified act whose `pc−1`\n   660\tis not a capture (`:captured-site`), a parked act whose `pc−1` is not\n   661\t`:park` (`:parked-site`).\n   662\t\n   663\t### 5.3 Engines and lanes\n   664\t\n   665\t**DECIDED** (frozen §10 phase 6: \"not the semantic profile alone\").\n   666\tThree lanes: `:semantic-register` (the reference: its wait entries *are*\n   667\tcanonical frames plus engine fields), `:stack-through-layout`,\n   668\t`:register-through-layout`. Every row runs on every lane. The de Bruijn\n   669\tlanes load `(:image (derive/stack-image v))` and\n   670\t`(:image (derive/register-image v))` of `v = (:vector (project P))`\n   671\tthrough `dvm/create-vm`/`rvm/create-vm` (as `v2_support/load-ast` does\n   672\twith the old lowerers, `v2_support.cljc:127-141`), run to the safepoint,\n   673\tand lift through `layout/lift-frame`.\n   674\t\n   675\t### 5.4 The laws, per row and lane\n   676\t\n   677\t1. **Reference parity.** The lowered machine, satisfied through the\n   678\t   source's streams, halts with the reference run's result and effect\n   679\t   trace (`reference` / `handed-off`, `:368-401`, kept).\n   680\t2. **Round trip.** `lift(lower(frame)) = frame` by root id after\n   681\t   stream-blinding (`v2_support/stream-blind`, `:531-543`), under the\n   682\t   fresh-receiver context of the draft's §9.\n   683\t3. **Observed reason.** the frame's pending reason is the wait's\n   684\t   observed reason, never the static kind (ucf-revisions §8).\n   685\t4. **Cross-engine canonical equality** (new, the law ruling 6 makes\n   686\t   possible): for one program at one safepoint, the canonical row sets\n   687\t   lifted from the three lanes are **equal by root id** after\n   688\t   stream-blinding and under controlled composition identities\n   689\t   (occurrence, origin, resource descriptors fixed by the harness).\n   690\t   This is the strongest statement of \"one truth, many interpretations\"\n   691\t   the phase can test: the same `act`, the same window, the same `K`,\n   692\t   the same `E`, whatever kernel held it.\n   693\t5. **Cross-engine lowering.** a row set lifted on one lane lowers on\n   694\t   each of the other two and continues to the reference result (the\n   695\t   6 ordered pairs).\n   696\t6. **Validator agreement.** every frame of every lifted row set passes\n   697\t   `frame/defect` in its context; every tampered row of §5.2 is refused\n   698\t   with the named kind; the validator's verdict is identical whichever\n   699\t   lane produced the frame.\n   700\t\n   701\t### 5.5 Observables and normalisation\n   702\t\n   703\t**DECIDED** (phase-5 §6.1.2 `native-normalize`, reused). Results and\n   704\teffect traces are compared under one normalisation applied to every\n   705\tside: host-typed values unwrapped; a closure (host type or `{:type\n   706\t:closure}` map) → `:closure` (a canonical closure carries `params` and a\n   707\tnamed `env`, a de Bruijn one arity and frames; only closure-ness is\n   708\tcommon to a value that crossed between them); a continuation →\n   709\t`:continuation`; stream and cursor refs → `{:type t :id id}`; host fns →\n   710\t`:host-fn`; collections recursively. Equality of **frames** (laws 2 and\n   711\t4) is by row-set root id, which is exact and needs no normalisation\n   712\tbeyond stream-blinding.\n   713\t\n   714\t### 5.6 Static checks the harness runs once per corpus segment\n   715\t\n   716\t1. `frame/defect` on every frame the reference lane mints: nil.\n   717\t2. For every parking pc `p` of `v`: `(analysis/saved a (inc p) rd)` has\n   718\t   no member `≥ k(body(p))` and does not contain `rd`.\n   719\t3. Register layout: `phys→virt(p, s)` is single-valued at every pc `p`\n   720\t   and every physical slot `s` of `L(p) ∪ def(p−1)`'s image; the live\n   721\t   operand of every boundary instruction of `R` equals the sorted\n   722\t   physical image of `saved(p+1, rd)`.\n   723\t4. Stack layout: the k-th non-push instruction of `H` has the mnemonic\n   724\t   family of `v[k]` (`:var` ↔ `:load-bound`/`:load-free`, `:closure` ↔\n   725\t   `:closure`, else equal mnemonics) for every `k`; counts agree.\n   726\t5. Stack layout: `(set (stack-layout p)) = (analysis/saved a (inc p) rd)`\n   727\t   for every parking pc `p`.\n   728\t6. `E` reconstruction: at every safepoint reached, the layout's `E`\n   729\t   equals the reference lane's `E` (as maps, values normalised).\n   730\t7. Closure reconstruction: canonical ↔ positional closures round-trip on\n   731\t   the `\"closure value\"` and `\"higher order\"` B0 rows and on\n   732\t   `:duplicate-param`.\n   733\t\n   734\t---\n   735\t\n   736\t## 6. Code in the carrier: A and the tree association\n   737\t\n   738\t### 6.1 What travels for code\n   739\t\n   740\t**DECIDED** (ruling 1, ruling 3, ruling 4; phase-5 §7.6 and §9.2; v2\n   741\tamendment §4's 2026-10-10 amendment: \"`:yin.k/code` and `:yin.k/requires\n   742\t:yin.k/segments` are keyed by the semantic A for all profiles; H and R\n   743\tare not keys\"). The root's `code` slot is plain `{A canonical-vector}`:\n   744\tevery vector a `\"v4\"` register-shaped vector that `code/well-formed?`\n   745\taccepts, keyed by its own `ucf/code-address`, verified on lower\n   746\t(draft §8 step 4). **No native image travels**: a stack or register\n   747\treceiver derives `H(A)`/`R(A)` with `derive/stack-image`/`register-image`\n   748\tafter admitting A, and may verify held bytes against that derivation\n   749\t(the frozen §4.3 \"through their layouts\" and the phase-5 lowering). The\n   750\tcarrier therefore has one code grammar for every receiver.\n   751\t\n   752\t`requires` carries UCF §7.6.1's map **plus** `:yin.k/trees {A #{tree-address …}}`,\n   753\tone entry per address in `:yin.k/segments`, the emitter's `source-index`\n   754\tentry (phase-5 §9.2: \"a UCF value with a segment in `:yin.k/segments`\n   755\tand no `:yin.k/trees` entry is `:yin.k/missing :yin.k/trees` and\n   756\tdiscovery `:incomplete`\"). The tree itself does not travel; it is\n   757\tretrievable by address, which is what unitarity asks. The derivations of\n   758\tnative images do not read it; the scanners (phase 5 §7) may.\n   759\t\n   760\t### 6.2 Rows, not datoms\n   761\t\n   762\t**DECIDED** (ruling 4). The carrier never projects a vector to datoms\n   763\tand never carries a datom batch for code. Code-as-tuples §7.2's\n   764\t\"projection path\" (vector → datoms → loader) is retired (§10.4); the\n   765\tdirect path is the only path, and the two AST projection lanes plus the\n   766\tdirect vector load feed one validator (frozen §3.4). Walker code (AST\n   767\trows) is outside this carrier: the walker is not a frame reconstructor\n   768\t(§4.1).\n   769\t\n   770\t### 6.3 The free environment\n   771\t\n   772\t**PROPOSED.** A canonical `E` includes the task's initial free\n   773\tenvironment (the `:env` a `create-vm` received, `semantic_register.cljc:261`),\n   774\tmerged under the lexical bindings (§4.4). A de Bruijn task holds that\n   775\tsame map as its task-wide `:free-env` (v2 amendment §2). The carrier\n   776\tcarries it **inside each `E`** as today's semantic lift does (every `E`\n   777\tis a complete map; sharing is Merkle, so one `:bindings` row serves\n   778\tevery frame with the same bindings), and carries no separate `free-env`\n   779\tslot: the root of the draft §5.5 therefore has no `free-env` and no\n   780\t`layout` (those were the positional profiles'). A de Bruijn receiver\n   781\tlowering a canonical `E` splits it back into its frames by the chain\n   782\t(§4.4) and recovers the free part as `E` minus the chain's bindings.\n   783\t\n   784\t---\n   785\t\n   786\t## 7. Lift and lower\n   787\t\n   788\t### 7.1 Lift\n   789\t\n   790\t**DECIDED** (draft §9, UCF §7.8): refuse unless quiescent\n   791\t(`:yin.k/not-quiescent`); refuse the holds (`:observe`, unminted cursor,\n   792\tpending close, cursorless `:link-request`) as `:yin.k/non-portable`\n   793\t`:reason-mismatch` (`unliftable-hold`, `handoff.cljc:588`); classify kind\n   794\t(`:parked` when `:value` is a parked record held in `:parked`;\n   795\t`:halted`; `:blocked` when the wait set is non-empty; else\n   796\t`:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`); run the dependency closure\n   797\t(`completion/complete` over the register-shaped vectors through the\n   798\tphase-5 scanners, `scan/requirements`, `scan/free-names`) and refuse\n   799\t`:yin.k/unsatisfied` unless `:complete`; number cells (draft §6); walk\n   800\twaits (each `act`/`tail` payload → `:act`/`:tail` rows, its engine fields\n   801\t→ the `:pending` row), parked records, the store slice, module stores,\n   802\tthe result, install children; run `frame/defect` over every frame; emit\n   803\trows and the census; the root's id is the body address.\n   804\t\n   805\tFor a de Bruijn source, the walk is the same over the frames\n   806\t`layout/lift-frame` reconstructs; the kernel's own export code\n   807\t(`handoff.cljc`'s version-2 adapters) is not used.\n   808\t\n   809\t### 7.2 Lower\n   810\t\n   811\t**DECIDED** (draft §8 in order, with step 7 replaced by §3.3): gate\n   812\t(version 3, profile `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`),\n   813\tstructure, graph, hashes (every content row, every code vector to its\n   814\tA), canonical form, canonical numbering, **frames** (`frame/defect` on\n   815\tevery state row in its context), pending and operations, dependency\n   816\tclosure (`requires` and `code` agree with the census; `:yin.k/trees`\n   817\tcomplete), custody, composition, restore. Restore builds the receiving\n   818\tkernel's state: for the semantic-register kernel, `code` through\n   819\t`load-vector`/`attach-image` under `code/contract`, each `:wait` back to\n   820\tan engine entry (`act`/`tail` payload plus the pending's engine fields,\n   821\t`lower-frame!`'s shapes, `handoff.cljc:3182-3246`, with `:deliver`\n   822\tcarried), parked records into `:parked`, the result into `:value`; for a\n   823\tde Bruijn kernel, `derive` the native image from each A, attach it, and\n   824\t`layout/lower-frame` each frame into the kernel's payload shape.\n   825\tRestoration delivers no value, runs nothing, mints nothing.\n   826\t\n   827\t---\n   828\t\n   829\t## 8. Slices, gates, entry conditions\n   830\t\n   831\tVerification follows `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`: G0 per iteration on\n   832\tthe JVM, G1 `bb test:sub yin.vm` on three hosts at the checkpoint, G2\n   833\t`bb test:changed`, G3 on master. New namespaces are under `yin.vm` by\n   834\tprefix; the Node log must show `Testing <ns>` for each new test\n   835\tnamespace.\n   836\t\n   837\t### 8.1 Slice 6a: the frame validator and the row codec\n   838\t\n   839\t**Files to create.**\n   840\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc` (§3): `defect`,\n   841\t  `saved-of` (the recomputation), public.\n   842\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` (§2): the row table as data,\n   843\t  `frame->rows`, `rows->frame`, `encode-row-id` (Jing default digest),\n   844\t  the cell census and numbering per the draft §6 (ported from the draft's\n   845\t  specification; nothing of `handoff.cljc` is edited), `lift-task`,\n   846\t  `lower-task` for the semantic-register kernel, body version 3.\n   847\t- `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame_test.cljc`,\n   848\t  `test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc`.\n   849\t\n   850\t**Depends on:** phase 3 (landed), 4a (landed), 4b stage 1 (streams,\n   851\tpark, resume, current-continuation: `srvm-phase4b`) for the live rows\n   852\tit lifts; FFI and link rows wait for 4b stage 2 and are 6b's.\n   853\t**Touches nothing of 4b or 5.**\n   854\t\n   855\t**Acceptance (6a).**\n   856\t\n   857\t1. `frame-test/rules-are-independent-of-engine`: `frame/defect` takes a\n   858\t   keyed frame and a code map only; its namespace requires no kernel\n   859\t   namespace (asserted by inspecting the `ns` form's requires in the\n   860\t   test, a string check over the source file read as a resource on the\n   861\t   JVM lane, `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)`).\n   862\t2. `frame-test/every-reference-frame-validates`: for every program of\n   863\t   the phase-5 corpus `C` that parks on 4b stage 1 (the blocked-read,\n   864\t   blocked-write, park and capture rows over the four segments of\n   865\t   §5.2), every `act`, `tail`, return frame, parked record and reified\n   866\t   value the register evaluator mints passes `defect` in its context.\n   867\t3. `frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper`: for each of rules 1-14 one\n   868\t   tampered frame built from a valid one, refused with that rule's kind\n   869\t   and a path naming the slot; fourteen rows, each named by kind.\n   870\t4. `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member`: a program whose live\n   871\t   register holds nil at the safepoint (`(f (stream-next c) nil-reg)`\n   872\t   with `[:const r nil]` evaluated before the read) validates with the\n   873\t   key present; the same frame with the key filtered out is\n   874\t   `:window-missing`.\n   875\t5. `frame-test/worked-example-saved`: on `:worked-example`'s vector, a\n   876\t   frame at pc 4 with window `{1 <f>}` and `rd 2` validates; `{1 <f> 2 x}`\n   877\t   is `:window-self`; `{}` is `:window-missing`; `{1 <f> 3 x}` is\n   878\t   `:window-extra` (`saved(4, 2) = {1}`, `analysis_test.cljc:131-139`).\n   879\t6. `rows-test/bijection`: `frame->rows ∘ rows->frame` and the converse\n   880\t   are identities on every frame of item 2, nil-valued keys included.\n   881\t7. `rows-test/row-ids-are-jing-default`: every content row's id equals\n   882\t   `(jing/segment-key body)` and names Jing's default algorithm\n   883\t   (`:segment/blake3-…`); no `sha256` appears in any id.\n   884\t8. `rows-test/one-profile`: a body whose profile map is anything but\n   885\t   `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`, including the four\n   886\t   version-2 maps, is `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` before any row is read;\n   887\t   a body with version 0, 1 or 2 likewise.\n   888\t9. `rows-test/lift-lower-round-trip`: for every 4b-stage-1 row of §5.2\n   889\t   over the four segments on the semantic-register kernel,\n   890\t   `lift(lower(S)) = S` by root id, and the lowered task continues to the\n   891\t   reference result.\n   892\t10. `rows-test/window-sorted-and-unique`: a `:window` row with keys out\n   893\t    of order or duplicated is `:yin.k/undecodable` at step 5 (canonical\n   894\t    form) naming the row.\n   895\t11. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n   896\t\n   897\t### 8.2 Slice 6b: the full harness on the reference kernel\n   898\t\n   899\t**Files to change.** `rows.cljc`: the FFI, link and install rows (the\n   900\tpending rows are already tabled; the lift walks the stage-2 entries).\n   901\t**Files to create.**\n   902\t`test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc`: §5 for the\n   903\t`:semantic-register` lane (the old harness file is not edited; it tests\n   904\tthe old machine until phase 8).\n   905\t\n   906\t**Depends on:** 4b stage 2 (FFI, link, install, `module/IModuleKernel`\n   907\tfor the register evaluator). Touches nothing of 4b or 5.\n   908\t\n   909\t**Acceptance (6b).**\n   910\t\n   911\t1. `every-row-every-segment-matches-the-reference`: the §5.2 rows ×\n   912\t   four segments on the reference lane; laws 1-3 and 6 of §5.4; counts\n   913\t   asserted (rows 15, segments 4).\n   914\t2. `tail-states-carry-no-window`: for the two tail rows and the\n   915\t   tail-effect halt, the lifted state row is `:tail` with three slots,\n   916\t   and the lowered task delivers through `K` (pops a frame, or halts\n   917\t   with an env free of `store-of`).\n   918\t3. `install-row-carries-the-child`: the install rows carry the child\n   919\t   task; lowering spawns no initialization and the waiter resumes with\n   920\t   the module symbol.\n   921\t4. `captures-round-trip-and-invoke`: the reified and nested-capture rows\n   922\t   lower, and invoking the lowered continuation delivers once into the\n   923\t   captured `rd` (the evaluator's `:continuation` arm).\n   924\t5. `refusals`: every refusal row of §5.2 refuses with the named status\n   925\t   and kind before any attachment (counting attachments as the old\n   926\t   harness does).\n   927\t6. `a-response-cursor-shared-by-two-waiters-crosses-as-one-cell` and\n   928\t   `a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent`, ported to the reference\n   929\t   lane.\n   930\t7. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts; the Node log\n   931\t   shows `Testing yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test`.\n   932\t\n   933\t### 8.3 Slice 6c: the two layouts and the cross-engine lanes\n   934\t\n   935\t**Files to create.** `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc`\n   936\t(§4); `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc`; the two extra\n   937\tlanes added to the 6b harness file.\n   938\t\n   939\t**Depends on:** phase 5a and 5b landed (`derive/stack-image`,\n   940\t`derive/register-image`); 6b. **Touches nothing of 5** (it calls\n   941\t`derive`'s public functions and reads the two kernels' public state).\n   942\t\n   943\t**Acceptance (6c).**\n   944\t\n   945\t1. `layout-test/register-pairing-is-total`: for every `P ∈ C`, every\n   946\t   virtual register of every body has a physical pair read off `(v, R)`,\n   947\t   and `phys→virt(p, s)` is single-valued at every pc (§5.6 item 3).\n   948\t2. `layout-test/register-live-is-the-saved-image`: §5.6 item 3, second\n   949\t   clause, for every boundary pc of every `P ∈ C`.\n   950\t3. `layout-test/stack-correspondence`: §5.6 item 4 for every `P ∈ C`.\n   951\t4. `layout-test/stack-layout-is-the-saved-set`: §5.6 item 5 for every\n   952\t   parking pc of every `P ∈ C`; and the two worked cases pinned:\n   953\t   `(f (g x) y)` inner call → `[1]`; `(f (if c (g) 2) y)` at `(g)` → `[1]`.\n   954\t5. `layout-test/env-reconstruction`: §5.6 item 6 over the harness rows\n   955\t   and the `:duplicate-param`, `:nested-closure`, `:nested-lambdas`\n   956\t   programs.\n   957\t6. `layout-test/closures-round-trip`: §5.6 item 7.\n   958\t7. `harness/cross-engine-canonical-equality`: §5.4 law 4 for every row ×\n   959\t   segment: the three lanes' row sets are equal by root id after\n   960\t   stream-blinding.\n   961\t8. `harness/cross-engine-lowering`: §5.4 law 5, the six ordered lane\n   962\t   pairs, every row × segment, reference parity.\n   963\t9. `harness/layout-refusals`: `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` from a kernel\n   964\t   stepped to a non-safepoint pc; a kernel state whose live operand was\n   965\t   tampered reconstructs a frame the validator refuses (`:window-extra`).\n   966\t10. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n   967\t\n   968\t### 8.4 Phase 7's entry conditions\n   969\t\n   970\t**DECIDED** (frozen §10 phase 7: \"Stage D/E rerun … over the new\n   971\ttransport, three hosts\"). Phase 7 may start when: 6a-6c are green on\n   972\tthree hosts; the row carrier is the only writer and reader the\n   973\tsemantic-register kernel has (`rows/lift-task`, `rows/lower-task`); the\n   974\tholder, checkpoint, ledger and authority paths (`yin.vm.ucf.holder.*`,\n   975\t`checkpoint.cljc`, `ledger.cljc`, `authority.cljc`) have a documented\n   976\tseam to call them (phase 7 wires it; phase 6 does not edit those\n   977\tnamespaces); and the Stage D/E scenarios\n   978\t(`test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e_scenarios.cljc`, `checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`)\n   979\thave been listed with, for each, the row of §5.2 that exercises its\n   980\tparking shape, so phase 7 re-encodes known shapes.\n   981\t\n   982\t### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n   983\t\n   984\t| | needs | concurrent with |\n   985\t|---|---|---|\n   986\t| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a, 5b, 5c |\n   987\t| 6b | 4b stage 2 | 5a, 5b, 5c |\n   988\t| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b | 5c |\n   989\t\n   990\tNo file of 4b (`semantic_register.cljc`, its tests, the four backend\n   991\tmaps) or of phase 5 (`derive.cljc`, `scan.cljc`, `linker.cljc`,\n   992\t`link.cljc`, their tests) is edited; `handoff.cljc` and the old harness\n   993\tare not edited (they test the stack-shaped machine and leave at phase\n   994\t8). The one shared seam is `module/IModuleKernel` on the register\n   995\tevaluator (4b stage 2's `link-format`, `lift-closure`, `lower-closure`),\n   996\twhich `rows.cljc` calls and does not define.\n   997\t\n   998\t---\n   999\t\n  1000\t## 9. Verification honesty\n  1001\t\n  1002\t- **Hand-derived numbers.** `saved(4, 2) = {1}` and `L(5) = {1,2,5}` on\n  1003\t  the worked example are the phase-3 tests' (`analysis_test.cljc:131-139`),\n  1004\t  not mine. The stack layout `[1]` at the inner call of `(f (g x) y)` and\n  1005\t  at `(g)` in `(f (if c (g) 2) y)` were derived by hand twice from the\n  1006\t  §4.3 walk and checked against those saved sets; the register layout's\n  1007\t  `phys(1) = 0` for the worked example follows from the phase-5 §6.3\n  1008\t  row 2 (`f` in `T0`), itself hand-derived there and confirmed by the\n  1009\t  reviewer. Nothing was run.\n  1010\t- **Claims that are checks, not theorems.** (i) the stack operand slice\n  1011\t  equals the saved window as a set (§4.3; §5.6 item 5); (ii) the\n  1012\t  non-push H sequence corresponds one-to-one with A (§4.3; item 4);\n  1013\t  (iii) `phys→virt` is single-valued per pc (§4.2; item 3); (iv) the\n  1014\t  layout's `E` equals the evaluator's `E` (§4.4; item 6). Each has an\n  1015\t  argument in its section and a corpus-wide test; the implementation\n  1016\t  relies on none of them silently.\n  1017\t- **Private access.** Every function a test names is public:\n  1018\t  `frame/defect`, `rows/frame->rows`, `rows/rows->frame`,\n  1019\t  `rows/lift-task`, `rows/lower-task`, `layout/register-layout`,\n  1020\t  `layout/stack-layout`, `layout/lift-frame`, `layout/lower-frame`,\n  1021\t  `derive/register-image`, `derive/stack-image`, `analysis/saved`,\n  1022\t  `code/parse`; no `#'` anywhere (`debruijn_register_contract_test.cljc:256-262`\n  1023\t  records why).\n  1024\t- **Universal claims avoided.** No sentence says every kernel can\n  1025\t  reconstruct a canonical frame; the two that are intended to are named\n  1026\t  and tested; the walker is excluded with the reason.\n  1027\t- **Unverified.** The 4b stage-2 shapes (FFI, link, install entries on\n  1028\t  the register evaluator) are specified from the evaluator design and\n  1029\t  the stage-1 branch; stage 2 is not landed, so 6b's rows are written\n  1030\t  against the design's §1.4-1.5 shapes and must be re-read when stage 2\n  1031\t  lands.\n  1032\t\n  1033\t---\n  1034\t\n  1035\t## 10. Findings and proposed amendments\n  1036\t\n  1037\t### 10.1 To the frozen design (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`)\n  1038\t\n  1039\t**F1 — §4.2 row names (PROPOSED).** The last paragraph says \"`:regs`\n  1040\tbecomes `[segment-A pc env-cref window-cref k-cref deliver-D]` for an\n  1041\t`act` and a sibling `:tail-state [segment-A site k-cref deliver-D]` is\n  1042\tadded\". Replace with: \"the frame rows are `:act [segment-A pc env-cref\n  1043\twindow-cref k-cref rd]` and `:tail [segment-A site k-cref]`, the kind\n  1044\tbeing the delivery discriminant (`:act` delivers to `rd`, `:tail`\n  1045\tthrough return), so `deliver` is not a slot; `:window` is a keyed row\n  1046\t`[r₁ V₁ r₂ V₂ …]` sorted by `r` in which a nil-valued register is a\n  1047\tpresent `[:lit nil]`; `:kframe` is `[segment-A pc env-cref window-cref\n  1048\trd]`; `:stack` and `stack-base` are removed. The amendment is\n  1049\t`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §2.\"\n  1050\t\n  1051\t**F2 — §4.2 \"the full frame validator\" (DECIDED, made exact).** After\n  1052\t\"and pending compatibility with `reason`\" insert: \"The fourteen rules,\n  1053\ttheir order and their refusal kinds are\n  1054\t`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §3.2; the validator is a\n  1055\tpure function of the decoded frame and the carried code and knows no\n  1056\tengine.\"\n  1057\t\n  1058\t**F3 — §4.3 foreign engines (DECIDED, made exact).** After \"`lift(lower(frame))\n  1059\t= frame` holds for admitted canonical frames, as today.\" insert: \"The\n  1060\tregister kernel's layout pairs physical and virtual registers pc by pc\n  1061\tfrom the two images `v` and `R(v)`, which share pcs; the stack kernel's\n  1062\tlayout corresponds the non-push instructions of `H(v)` with `v` and lays\n  1063\tthe saved window out as the activation's operand stack in emission\n  1064\torder; both kernels' positional frames become `E` through the owner\n  1065\tchain of A and `bind-params` (continuation design §4). The AST walker is\n  1066\tnot a frame reconstructor.\"\n  1067\t\n  1068\t**F4 — §10 phase 6 (DECIDED, made exact).** Replace \"the row carrier\n  1069\tamended\" with \"the row carrier amended to body version 3 with one\n  1070\tprofile, `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`, carrying\n  1071\tcanonical vectors by A and `:yin.k/trees`, never a native image\n  1072\t(continuation design §2, §6)\"; and after \"through their layouts\" insert\n  1073\t\"(the register and stack kernels; the walker is excluded)\".\n  1074\t\n  1075\t### 10.2 To UCF (`yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`)\n  1076\t\n  1077\t**U1 — §7.3.4 `:511`.** Replace \"`:yin.k/carried` carries vectors, not\n  1078\tbatches.\" with \"`:yin.k/carried` and the body's code map carry\n  1079\t**register-shaped canonical vectors keyed by A**, never batches, never\n  1080\tdatoms projected from a vector (the projection path is retired,\n  1081\tcode-as-tuples §7.2 as amended), and never a native stack or register\n  1082\timage: a receiver of either native kernel derives its image from A\n  1083\t(`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md` §2-3). `:yin.k/requires\n  1084\t:yin.k/trees` maps every address in `:yin.k/segments` to the set of tree\n  1085\taddresses the emitter's `source-index` held for it (derivations design\n  1086\t§9.2).\"\n  1087\t\n  1088\t**U2 — §7.4.1.** The frozen design §4.1 rewrote this section; add at\n  1089\tits head: \"Superseded for the register-shaped machine by\n  1090\t`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §4.1 (two state columns, `act` and\n  1091\t`tail`, and the `deliver` record); the table below describes the\n  1092\tstack-shaped machine, which leaves at that design's phase 8.\" Replace\n  1093\tthe `:yin.k/frame` example with the §1.2 keyed form of this document.\n  1094\t\n  1095\t**U3 — §7.4.2.** Replace \"`[sp :yin.safepoint/stack-effect -1]`\" with\n  1096\t\"`[sp :yin.safepoint/def #{…}] [sp :yin.safepoint/use #{…}] [sp\n  1097\t:yin.safepoint/live #{…}]`  ; def(pc), use(pc), L(pc) derived from A\n  1098\t(frozen §8.1)\" and the rule \"`stack-effect` and `lexically-required` are\n  1099\tderived from the canonical vector alone\" with \"`def`, `use`, `live` and\n  1100\t`lexically-required` are derived from the canonical vector alone\n  1101\t(`yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis`)\". Replace \"E, St, and every K\n  1102\tframe's `:stack-base` and env travel in the value\" with \"E, the saved\n  1103\twindow, and every K frame's window, `rd` and env travel in the value\".\n  1104\tReplace \"`:yin.safepoint/layout` … physical slot → canonical slot\" with\n  1105\t\"physical location → virtual register (continuation design §4)\".\n  1106\t\n  1107\t**U4 — §7.4.3.** Add after \"Three rules make these resumable\": \"A\n  1108\tpending rides on an `act` state (write-result delivery) or a `tail`\n  1109\tstate (through-return delivery); the variants are unchanged, and\n  1110\t`:yin.k/registers R` of the version-2 amendment is the `act`/`tail`\n  1111\tstate of the frozen design §4.2.\" No variant changes.\n  1112\t\n  1113\t**U5 — §7.6.** In §7.6.1's `:yin.k/requires` example add the line\n  1114\t`:yin.k/trees {A #{tree-address …}}  ; §7.6.1a, every segment's source trees`\n  1115\tand a new paragraph **§7.6.1a The source association**: the phase-5\n  1116\t§9.2 UCF row text, verbatim.\n  1117\t\n  1118\t**U6 — §7.11.** In \"Safepoint conformance harness\" replace \"including\n  1119\t`lift ∘ lower = id`, the static `stack-effect`/`lexically-required`\n  1120\tchecks\" with \"including `lift ∘ lower = id`, the static `def`/`use`/`L`\n  1121\tand `lexically-required` checks, the frame validator on every frame,\n  1122\tand **cross-engine canonical equality**: one program at one safepoint\n  1123\tlifts to one canonical row set from the semantic-register kernel and\n  1124\tfrom the stack and register kernels through their layouts (continuation\n  1125\tdesign §5.4 law 4)\". In §7.11.1 \"Safepoint reconstruction\", replace\n  1126\t\"Separately prepare two independently implemented UCF engines\" with\n  1127\t\"Separately prepare the three engines intended to reconstruct canonical\n  1128\tframes\" and \"the frame, pending wait, next result, and effect trace must\n  1129\tagree in both directions\" with \"the canonical row set, pending wait,\n  1130\tnext result and effect trace must agree across all three and in every\n  1131\tlowering direction\".\n  1132\t\n  1133\t### 10.3 To the row-carrier draft (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`)\n  1134\t\n  1135\t**R1 — §2.** Replace the section with: \"**Body version 3, one\n  1136\tprofile.** The carrier is body version 3. It reads no other version\n  1137\t(owner, 2026-10-11: no legacy). The profile map is `{:yin.code/contract\n  1138\t\"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`, the canonical register-shaped machine's\n  1139\tcontract; there is no engine key, because the frame is the canonical\n  1140\tmachine's and the kernel that executes it is the receiving composition's\n  1141\tchoice (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §2.1). A body\n  1142\tnaming any other profile is `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`.\"\n  1143\t\n  1144\t**R2 — §5.2.** Replace the table and paragraph with §2.3 of this\n  1145\tdocument (the `:act`, `:tail`, `:window`, `:k`, `:kframe`, `:wait`\n  1146\trows) and its notes.\n  1147\t\n  1148\t**R3 — §5.1 `:reified`.** Replace `[:reified regs-cref]` with\n  1149\t`[:reified act-cref]` and \"its pc must be a `:current-continuation`\n  1150\tsite's successor, not a wait or park safepoint\" with \"its act's `pc−1`\n  1151\tis a `:current-continuation` and it has no pending (frame rule 13)\".\n  1152\t\n  1153\t**R4 — §5.4 `:parked-table`.** Replace `regs-cref` with `state-cref`\n  1154\t(`:act` or `:tail`) and add frame rule 14's bookkeeping clause.\n  1155\t\n  1156\t**R5 — §5.5 the root.** `contract` is the one profile map of R1; the\n  1157\troot has no `free-env` and no `layout` slot (continuation design §6.3);\n  1158\t`code` is `{A canonical-vector}` of `\"v4\"` vectors.\n  1159\t\n  1160\t**R6 — §8 step 7.** Replace with: \"**Frames.** Every `:act`, `:tail`,\n  1161\t`:kframe`, `:reified` and parked-table state is decoded to its keyed\n  1162\tframe and judged by `yin.vm.semantic-register.frame/defect` with its\n  1163\tcontext (`:wait`, `:captured`, `:parked`); a defect is\n  1164\t`:yin.k/undecodable` with the rule's kind and the row path\n  1165\t(continuation design §3).\"\n  1166\t\n  1167\t**R7 — \"the `v3` stamp does not move\" (§2, §10.4).** Delete; the code\n  1168\tstamp is `\"v4\"` and the carrier version is 3; neither statement about\n  1169\tversions 0-2 survives.\n  1170\t\n  1171\t**R8 — §9 \"Legacy correspondence\" and §10.3 \"the nested grammar\".**\n  1172\tDelete: there is no legacy reader and no nested projection; rows are the\n  1173\tone carrier.\n  1174\t\n  1175\t**R9 — §10.7 \"other profile tables\".** Delete: there are no other\n  1176\tprofiles; the stack and register kernels reconstruct canonical frames\n  1177\t(§4).\n  1178\t\n  1179\t### 10.4 To code-as-tuples (`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`) §7.2\n  1180\t\n  1181\t**C1.** Replace the first paragraph (\"This section supersedes the\n  1182\tsentence in UCF §7.3.4 … Everything else in §7.3.4 stands.\") with: \"The\n  1183\tvector-to-datoms projection path is **retired** (owner ruling of\n  1184\t2026-09-18, recorded in `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §3.4 'One vector\n  1185\tvalidator'). There is one load path for a vector, the direct one, and\n  1186\ttwo AST projection lanes (datom lane, row lane) that produce the vector;\n  1187\tall three feed one validator (`yin.vm.semantic-register.code/well-formed?`).\n  1188\tUCF §7.3.4's projection path is superseded accordingly.\" Replace\n  1189\tobligation 2's second sentence (\"loading the instruction vector directly\n  1190\tand loading its datom projection yield the same image\") with \"loading\n  1191\tthe vector produced by either AST lane and the vector loaded directly\n  1192\tyield the same image and address (`load_paths_test.cljc`)\", and\n  1193\tobligation 3's \"both paths refuse with the same defect\" with \"the\n  1194\tdirect vector load refuses with the published defect (rule and pc) for\n  1195\tevery rule of `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §3.4\". Obligations 1 and\n  1196\t4 stand.\n  1197\t\n  1198\t### 10.5 Checked and consistent (no amendment)\n  1199\t\n  1200\tFrozen §2.4 delivery shapes against the 4b branch (`act-payload`,\n  1201\t`tail-builders`, `:deliver` record); frozen §4.1 two state columns; the\n  1202\tevaluator design §1.3-1.6 shapes; the draft's §3, §4, §5.1 (except\n  1203\t`:reified`), §5.3, §6, §7 and §8 steps 1-6, 8-12; v2 amendment §2's `E`\n  1204\tshape (reused as the `:env` row); the phase-5 §9.2 `:yin.k/trees` text.\n  1205\t\n  1206\t---\n  1207\t\n  1208\t## 11. Owner questions\n  1209\t\n  1210\t**None.** Two design choices are the Architect reviewer's: dropping\n  1211\t`:yin.k/engine` from the profile map (§2.1) and carrying the free\n  1212\tenvironment inside every `E` rather than as a root slot (§6.3). Both\n  1213\tfollow from ruling 6 as this document reads it; the reviewer may prefer\n  1214\tan explicit engine tag for diagnostics without changing any gate.\n  1215\t\n  1216\t---\n  1217\t\n  1218\t## 12. Portability notes for the implementer\n  1219\t\n  1220\t1. **Nil-valued window keys (Dart, Node).** The window is built with\n  1221\t   `select-keys` and encoded as `[r [:lit nil]]`; never filter `some?`\n  1222\t   values, never `(into {} (filter val …))`; `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member`\n  1223\t   is the canary. `(get W r)` is nil for absent and for nil alike, so\n  1224\t   membership is always by `contains?`/key sets.\n  1225\t2. **`for` over large seqs (Dart).** Row sets of the C4 modules run to\n  1226\t   thousands of rows; build with `mapv`/`into`/`reduce`.\n  1227\t3. **Reader whitespace before closers (Dart).** Pinned row sets and\n  1228\t   fixtures are Clojure data in `.cljc`, never EDN strings.\n  1229\t4. **Duplicate protocol params (Dart).** `gc-children [_ _x]`\n  1230\t   (`srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:391`); any new protocol method\n  1231\t   in `layout` likewise.\n  1232\t5. **Multi-key `assoc` on nil (Dart).** Frames and windows start from\n  1233\t   `{}`; `(assoc nil :a 1 :b 2)` is a list on Dart (`handoff.cljc:1455-1457`\n  1234\t   records the trap).\n  1235\t6. **Reader conditionals.** `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`\n  1236\t   with `:cljd` first; `:clj`-only source-reading tests as\n  1237\t   `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)`.\n  1238\t7. **Private var access (Dart).** Every function named in §8 is public;\n  1239\t   no `#'`.\n  1240\t8. **Sorted keys.** Window rows and bindings rows are sorted by Jing\n  1241\t   canonical bytes of the key, never by host `sort` on mixed types;\n  1242\t   integers sort numerically under canonical CBOR.\n  1243\t9. **Numeric classes (Node).** `pc`, `rd`, `r` are exact integers;\n  1244\t   compare with `cbor/numeric-kind` before `=` where a value came off the\n  1245\t   wire (`ucf/profile-engine`, `ucf.cljc:77-91`, is the template).\n  1246\t10. **Fresh worktree.** `mise trust` and `npm ci` before the Node lane.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
